_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 34
---
order: 34
---
short_label: XI.34
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: In equal parallelepipedal solids the bases are reciprocally proportional to the heights; and those parallelepipedal solids in which the bases are reciprocally proportional to the heights are equal.
----
proof:

Let {AB|sAB} and {CD|sCD} be equal parallelepipedal solids.

I say that in the parallelepipedal solids {AB|sAB} and {CD|sCD} the bases are reciprocally proportional to the heights, that is the base {EH|pEH} is to the base {NQ|pNQ} as the height of the solid {CD|sCD} is to the height of the solid {AB|sAB}.

First, let the sides which stand up, namely {AG}, {EF}, {LB}, {HK}, {CM}, {NO}, {PD}, and {QR}, be at right angles to their bases.

I say that the base {EH|pEH} is to the base {NQ|pNQ} as {CM} is to {AG}.

