                  { elem: "aYWX", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outline } ] } },
            { text: "I say that, in this case too, if the solids {AB|sAB} and {CD|sCD} are equal,",
              visible: SOL1,
              highlighted: ["sAB","sCD"] },
            { text: "then the bases are reciprocally proportional to the heights,",
              visible: SOL1,
              highlighted: ["pEH","pNQ","GT","MX"] },
            { text: "that is, the base {EH|pEH} is to the base {NQ|pNQ} as the height of the solid {CD|sCD} to the height of the solid {AB|sAB}.",
              visible: SOL1,
              highlighted: ["pEH","pNQ","MX","GT"] },
            { text: "Since the solid {AB|sAB} equals the solid {CD|sCD}, and {AB|sAB} equals {BT|sFV},",
              visible: SOL1,
              highlighted: ["sAB","sCD","sFV"] },
            { text: "for they are on the same base {FK|pFK} and of the same height,",
              visible: SOL1,
              highlighted: ["pFK","GT"] },
            { text: "and the solid {CD|sCD} equals {DX|sOa}, for they are again on the same base {RO|pRO} and of the same height,",
