              highlighted: ["sAB","sCD","sFV","sOa","GT","MX"] },
            { text: "therefore the base {FK|pFK} is to the base {OR|pRO} as the height of the solid {DX|sOa} is to the height of the solid {BT|sFV}.",
              visible: SOL1,
              highlighted: ["pFK","pRO","MX","GT"] },
            { text: "Therefore in the parallelepipedal solids {BT|sFV} and {DX|sOa} the bases are reciprocally proportional to the heights.",
              visible: SOL1,
              highlighted: ["sFV","sOa"] },
            { text: "Therefore the solid {BT|sFV} equals the solid {DX|sOa}.",
              visible: SOL1,
              highlighted: ["sFV","sOa"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "solid BT = solid DX", ref: "Above" }] },
            { text: "But {BT|sFV} equals {BA|sAB}, for they are on the same base {FK|pFK} and of the same height,",
              visible: SOL1,
              highlighted: ["sFV","sAB","pFK"] },
            { text: "and the solid {DX|sOa} equals the solid {DC|sCD}.",
              visible: SOL1,
